ormat="epo"><addressbook><name>MORITA KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGAWA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUDO, MITSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORITA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A plate spring-like feeding terminal (43) of a coreless motor (1) is obliquely fixed and extended upward toward the inside.  A motor holder (2) has a slope (23) going up toward the inside from an insert port (22).  Thereby, the feeding terminal (43) is protruded to the outside of the slope (23) when the motor (1) is inserted into the holder (2).  As a result, when the motor (1) and the holder (2) are incorporated into a portable communication terminal, the terminal (43) is pressed and electrically connected to a feeding circuit of a circuit board positioned above the terminal without any extra work such as soldering.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Une borne d'alimentation en forme de ressort à lame (43) d'un moteur sans noyau (1) est fixée à l'oblique et s'étend vers le haut, vers l'intérieur. Un support de moteur (2) possède une pente (23) s'étendant vers l'intérieur, depuis un port d'insertion (22). Ainsi, la borne d'alimentation (43) saille vers l'extérieur de la pente (23) lorsque le moteur (1) est inséré dans le support (2). Lorsque le moteur (1) et son support (2) sont intégrés dans un terminal de communication portatif, la borne (43) est comprimée et mise en contact électrique avec un circuit d'alimentation d'une carte de circuit positionnée au-dessus de la borne, sans qu'aucune opération supplémentaire, telle que le brasage, soit nécessaire.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>